We only do something special if you're using LongPolling.
And I just tested this out, and looks like there is an issue with how we clone the `WindowsPrincipal`.

As a workaround you can do:
```
var authState = await AuthenticationStateProvider.GetAuthenticationStateAsync();
if (authState.User.Identity is WindowsIdentity)
{
    isInGroup = new WindowsPrincipal((WindowsIdentity)authState.User.Identity).IsInRole("Users");
}
else
{
    isInGroup = authState.User.IsInRole("Users");
}
```

